==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
Topographic surname, from {{der|en|enm|went||crossroad, passage}}.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|~|s}}

# {{surname|en|from=Middle English}}.
# The {{w|River Went}}, {{place|en|a=a|river|co/West Yorkshire|co/North Yorkshire|co/South Yorkshire|and|co/East Riding of Yorkshire|cc/England|a tributary of the River|riv/Don}}. It forms the boundary between South Yorkshire and both North Yorkshire and the East Riding in its lower reaches.

====Derived terms====
* {{q|river}} {{l|en|Wentbridge}}

====Statistics====
* According to the 2010 United States Census, ''Went'' is the 58337<sup>th</sup> most common surname in the United States, belonging to 348 individuals. ''Went'' is most common among White (80.46%) and Black/African American (11.21%) individuals.

